    "text": "To determine the probability that a randomly chosen line connecting two distinct vertices of a regular dodecahedron lies inside the dodecahedron, we need to analyze the structure and properties of the dodecahedron.\n\n### Step-by-Step Analysis:\n\n1. **Vertices and Edges:**\n   - A regular dodecahedron has 20 vertices and 30 edges.\n\n2. **Total Number of Line Segments:**\n   - The total number of ways to choose 2 distinct vertices from 20 vertices is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{20}{2} \\):\n   \\[\n   \\binom{20}{2} = \\frac{20 \\times 19}{2} = 190\n   \\]\n   - Thus, there are 190 line segments connecting pairs of vertices.\n\n3. **Edges of the Dodecahedron:**\n   - The dodecahedron has 30 edges, which are the line segments that lie on the surface of the dodecahedron.\n\n4. **Line Segments Inside the Dodecahedron:**\n   - The remaining line segments are those that lie inside the dodecahedron. To find this number, we subtract the number of edges from the total number of line segments:\n   \\[\n   190 - 30 = 160\n   \\]\n\n5. **Probability Calculation:**\n   - The probability \\( P \\) that a randomly chosen line segment lies inside the dodecahedron is the ratio of the number of line segments inside the dodecahedron to the total number of line segments:\n   \\[\n   P = \\frac{\\text{Number of line segments inside}}{\\text{Total number of line segments}} = \\frac{160}{190} = \\frac{16}{19}\n   \\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{16}{19}}\n\\]",
